  "description": "A child's errand is given the scale of an epic. A boy takes the wrong notebook home from school and walks to the next village to return it before his friend is expelled; every adult is a locked door. It may be the simplest film imaginable and also the most suspenseful — proof that simplicity can hit as hard as complexity.\n\nEight-year-old Ahmed has mistakenly taken his friend Mohammad's notebook. He wants to return it, or else his friend will be expelled from school. The boy determinedly sets out to find Mohammad's home in the neighbouring village.",
